        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="1059" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg979"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Pioda.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 327.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, with reference to similar
                    previous correspondence, to inclose for your information copy of a dispatch from
                    the agent and consul-general of the United States at Cairo, and copy of an
                    instruction in reply, relative to the protection requested by Paul Dick, a
                    citizen of Switzerland, living in Cairo.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



